SUIT FOR PERMANENT INJUNCTION RESTRAINING INTERFERENCE WITH POSSESSION AND EASEMENT

MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:

1. That the Plaintiff is the absolute owner and in peaceful possession of residential House No. 22, Patel Nagar, Udaipur, more particularly described in Schedule-A (hereinafter “the suit property”). The Plaintiff and her predecessors have been in continuous, uninterrupted possession for more than 30 years.

2. That on the eastern side of the suit property there exists a 10-ft wide open passage which has been used by the Plaintiff and her family as a right of way / easement of necessity and by prescription for more than 20 years for access to the main road, parking, and for light and air.

3. That the Defendant is the owner of the adjoining House No. 23. Recently the Defendant has started digging foundation pits and stacking construction material on and near the said passage with the clear intention of constructing a wall / structure that will completely block the passage and obstruct the Plaintiff’s access, light and air.

4. That the Plaintiff issued a legal notice dated ______ calling upon the Defendant to desist. The Defendant has refused and continues the construction activity.

5. That the Plaintiff has a strong prima facie case, the balance of convenience is in her favour, and she will suffer irreparable injury if the Defendant is not restrained. The interference cannot be adequately compensated in terms of money.

6. That the cause of action arose when the Defendant commenced digging and stacking material, and is continuing day to day.

7. That the suit is valued at ₹ ______ for the purpose of court fee and jurisdiction. Fixed court fee has been paid.

PRAYER

It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon’ble Court may be pleased to:

(a) Pass a decree of permanent injunction restraining the Defendant, his agents, servants and any person claiming through him from interfering with the Plaintiff’s peaceful possession of the suit property and from obstructing, blocking or constructing any structure on or over the 10-ft wide passage described in Schedule-B, and from interfering with the Plaintiff’s right of way, light and air;

(b) Award costs of the suit; and

(c) Pass any other order as this Hon’ble Court may deem fit and proper.

Place: Udaipur
Date: _______________

                                                      Plaintiff
                                                      Through Counsel

